---
import Legal from '../layouts/Legal.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
---

<Legal
  title="Privacy"
  description="What Final Commit collects, why, and what it never does with your data."
  updated="7 October 2026"
>
  <h2>What we collect</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>What you send us on WhatsApp, by email or on a call: your name, course, college, deadline and your project idea.</li>
    <li>Files you share for your project, such as your college's report template or your guide's base paper.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>This website</h2>
  <p>
    Nothing you type into the "your idea" form is saved on this website. Pressing the button only opens WhatsApp or your email app with
    the message written; you decide whether to send it.
  </p>
  <p>
    We count visits and button taps with Umami, an analytics tool that doesn't use cookies and doesn't identify you. It tells us things
    like how many people opened a page and how many tapped the WhatsApp button, never who they were.
  </p>

  <h2>How we use it</h2>
  <p>
    Only to talk to you and to build and support your project. We don't sell your data, share it with anyone else, or add you to
    marketing lists. We never show your project to other students without your permission.
  </p>

  <h2>Your project repository</h2>
  <p>Your GitHub repository is private. Only you and the people you invite can see it.</p>

  <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
  <p>
    We keep your project files to support you until six months after your viva, then delete them. You can ask us to delete them earlier
    at any time.
  </p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    Under India's Digital Personal Data Protection Act, 2023, you can ask what we hold about you, ask us to correct it, or ask us to
    delete it. Message {site.phone} on WhatsApp or email {site.email}.
  </p>
</Legal>
